# downpipe environment variables (example)
#
# Copy to .env only if your shell sources it; the CLI reads these straight from
# the process environment and never writes them to disk. None are required to
# read, verify or restore from a local --archive directory: the recovery path is
# offline and makes no network call. Supply only the variables a given command
# needs. Never commit a real .env; only this .env.example is tracked.

# --- Reading from an S3-compatible source (--s3-endpoint / --s3-bucket) ---
# Where to get them: the access key pair for your destination bucket (R2,
# Backblaze B2, Wasabi, MinIO, AWS S3). Use a least-privilege, read-only key
# scoped to the one bucket. Rotate on the same schedule as the bucket itself,
# and revoke immediately if a workstation that held them is lost.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Provisioner path only: setup / preflight (read-only Cloudflare GETs) ---
# Where to get them: a Cloudflare API token scoped to the account you are
# standing the engine up in. setup and preflight use it for GET-only calls to
# api.cloudflare.com; the token stays on this machine and nothing is created or
# changed. Not used by any recovery command. Create it short-lived and delete it
# once onboarding is done; rotate at least every 90 days while in use.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
